WEBVTT

00:34.470 --> 00:38.690
Spice and Wolf

00:38.690 --> 00:39.810
Spice and Wolf

00:39.810 --> 00:45.150
Spice and Wolf

02:05.430 --> 02:10.440
<b>Episode 7
Scale of God and 
Sorcerer of the Grasslands</b>

02:09.870 --> 02:11.440
Well, aren't you well-off?

02:11.440 --> 02:13.520
I am hungry.

02:13.520 --> 02:15.290
You just ate some bread.

02:15.290 --> 02:18.990
Bread that hard and unpalatable does not count!

02:18.990 --> 02:21.700
If we bought enough food for you 
to feel full at every meal,

02:21.700 --> 02:24.080
we'd go bankrupt in one week.

02:24.080 --> 02:29.710
You can serve someone as cute as myself. 
Should you not feel honored as a male?

02:29.710 --> 02:32.910
How about I put that honor between 
some slices of bread and eat it.

02:34.150 --> 02:36.010
Do not puff up so.

02:36.010 --> 02:38.430
I'm not bread, so I can't puff up.

02:41.100 --> 02:42.340
So...

02:42.340 --> 02:44.810
How long until the next town?

02:49.350 --> 02:51.440
It should be right beyond that hill.

02:51.440 --> 02:54.300
I wonder what I will eat next.

02:54.300 --> 02:58.530
I would love to gnaw on a 
fresh and bloody cow or sheep.

02:58.530 --> 03:01.940
Something sweet on the side 
would perfect the meal.

03:01.940 --> 03:04.590
You ate a mountain of apple pies in Pazzio.

03:04.950 --> 03:07.280
After taking care of the apples 
you couldn't finish,

03:07.280 --> 03:10.660
I don't even want to smell 
sweet things for a while.

03:10.660 --> 03:12.580
They were delicious.

03:12.580 --> 03:16.550
Such an innovative way 
to eat them surprised me.

03:16.550 --> 03:21.070
Jeez, I hope you know that apples 
aren't processed for free.

03:21.590 --> 03:24.740
I'll be adding all the money 
you used to your tab...

03:35.890 --> 03:37.020
Is that it?

03:37.020 --> 03:38.480
Y-Yeah.

03:39.140 --> 03:40.490
That's Poroson.

03:45.950 --> 03:49.700
For there is only one God. 
He leads the people...

03:52.210 --> 03:54.580
What a boring town.

03:56.850 --> 03:59.250
Well, there aren't any food stalls open here.

03:59.250 --> 04:02.520
You make it seem as if 
I am only interested in food.

04:02.520 --> 04:04.570
Then, do you want to go 
listen to some preaching?

04:05.090 --> 04:08.410
They are five hundred years 
too young to preach to me.

04:08.410 --> 04:12.240
I think you'd benefit from listening 
to their preaching about frugality.

04:12.240 --> 04:15.060
I am a wolf.

04:15.060 --> 04:18.570
I do not understand such 
complicated things as preaching.

04:18.570 --> 04:21.650
Well, this town is probably the only place

04:21.650 --> 04:24.700
where preaching about frugality 
holds any weight.

04:26.070 --> 04:29.370
In the religious city of Ruvinheigen,

04:29.370 --> 04:32.040
the very bishop and priests 
that should follow those teachings

04:32.040 --> 04:34.290
are the most willing to fatten their wallets.

04:34.290 --> 04:36.700
The city is called Ruvinheigen?

04:36.700 --> 04:37.770
You recognize the name?

04:37.770 --> 04:42.300
Yes, though the name I heard
 was that of a person.

04:43.380 --> 04:46.180
Oh, you're not wrong.

04:46.180 --> 04:49.180
The city was named after the holy 
crusader, Saint Ruvinheigen,

04:49.180 --> 04:50.510
who fought against the pagans.

04:50.510 --> 04:54.170
It was the name of a man who had 
long flaming red hair and a beard,

04:54.170 --> 04:56.770
who always had a very austere expression.

04:56.770 --> 04:59.850
I believe that is how the saint 
is recorded in history.

04:59.850 --> 05:03.930
It was also said that his left arm was 
bitten off while fighting against a pagan god.

05:03.930 --> 05:05.290
His left arm?

05:05.780 --> 05:08.620
I only bit his arse.

05:09.280 --> 05:12.730
The moment he saw my cute ears and tail,

05:12.730 --> 05:16.170
he started screaming that I was 
a minion of the devil and chased me.

05:16.170 --> 05:21.420
He made me so angry 
I could not help but bite his arse.

05:22.210 --> 05:24.650
It was fibrous and not delicious at all.

05:27.220 --> 05:30.390
His arse, huh? Well, that's too embarrassing 
to leave in the history books.

05:31.190 --> 05:32.350
However, I must say.

05:33.810 --> 05:38.290
I only bit him. I did not end his life.

05:38.290 --> 05:40.220
You worry about strange things.

05:40.220 --> 05:41.770
It is important.

05:43.030 --> 05:44.110
Right.

05:45.140 --> 05:47.810
All right, let's head to the trading company.

05:47.810 --> 05:48.700
Yes.

05:48.700 --> 05:50.300
But first...

05:54.500 --> 05:55.910
Did you wait long?

06:03.320 --> 06:08.830
You looked like a nun in your robe, but now 
you totally look like a normal town girl.

06:08.830 --> 06:12.390
It would be difficult to find 
a town girl as cute as me.

06:13.260 --> 06:17.640
However, it seems there is not much point 
in showing me off in such a dull town.

06:17.980 --> 06:21.560
We'll head to Ruvinheigen after we sell 
this pepper to the Latparron Trading Company.

06:21.560 --> 06:22.910
Be patient until then.

06:27.890 --> 06:30.530
Is Ruvinheigen a large town?

06:30.530 --> 06:31.730
It's huge.

06:31.730 --> 06:34.810
It's more of a city than a town. 
There will be a lot of stalls.

06:34.810 --> 06:35.490
And apples?

06:36.030 --> 06:37.660
You really never get tired of them.

06:37.660 --> 06:40.510
Delicious things are delicious!

06:40.510 --> 06:42.000
So, how is it?

06:43.510 --> 06:45.650
I'm not sure about raw apples.

06:45.650 --> 06:49.120
It's about the time for them 
to be pickled for winter.

06:49.120 --> 06:50.360
Pickled?

06:50.360 --> 06:51.870
They pickle them in honey.

06:52.220 --> 06:56.050
They also pickle pears and sometimes 
peaches, on rare occasions.

06:56.050 --> 06:57.640
They're considered high class foods.

06:57.640 --> 07:01.400
They cut the peaches thinly and put 
figs and almonds between them.

07:02.180 --> 07:07.320
They generously pour honey over that 
and add a bit of ginger at the end.

07:08.990 --> 07:11.180
I had the opportunity to eat it once,

07:11.180 --> 07:14.300
but it was so sweet the Church 
debated banning it.

07:15.830 --> 07:17.900
Hey, you're drooling.

07:19.750 --> 07:22.600
I don't know if they'll be available though.

07:22.600 --> 07:26.040
They're usually reserved for the nobles or 
the rich, so they aren't normally in stores.

07:30.300 --> 07:31.760
If they are?

07:31.760 --> 07:34.240
Got it. I'll buy it for you.

07:34.240 --> 07:35.620
You swear it?

07:35.620 --> 07:37.280
Y-Yeah...

07:37.280 --> 07:39.590
Then, we must make haste!

07:41.850 --> 07:43.500
They may sell out.

07:43.500 --> 07:45.120
It would be terrible if that happened.

07:45.120 --> 07:46.940
This is peaches and honey we speak of.

07:47.200 --> 07:48.380
I cannot believe it.

07:48.380 --> 07:49.800
I cannot believe this at all!

07:49.800 --> 07:52.170
Only if they're being sold. Are you listening?

07:52.170 --> 07:54.700
But pears are difficult to ignore as well.

07:59.740 --> 08:05.130
Heretics and devils hide among us in town, 
looking like normal people.

08:05.130 --> 08:06.780
Just a few days ago,

08:06.780 --> 08:12.170
they found a sorcerer living among them that 
could control wolves near Ruvinheigen.

08:12.170 --> 08:15.860
However, the Church still reaches their 
benevolent hands toward people like that

08:15.860 --> 08:17.730
and forgives them.

08:19.940 --> 08:22.600
Well, then. Shall we get down to business?

08:23.700 --> 08:25.110
Please.

08:25.480 --> 08:28.980
So, what kind of product 
do you have for me today?

08:28.980 --> 08:30.340
This.

08:31.990 --> 08:34.400
Oh, pepper?

08:35.620 --> 08:37.280
I'm surprised you recognized it so easily.

08:37.280 --> 08:38.860
I could smell it.

08:38.860 --> 08:44.710
Then, let's weigh the product. 
Do you own a scale?

08:44.710 --> 08:46.340
No, I don't.

08:46.810 --> 08:49.910
However, I have faith in God.

08:52.500 --> 08:57.680
Even so, you brought pepper at a good time.

08:58.000 --> 09:01.390
The demand for pepper 
has increased drastically lately.

09:01.390 --> 09:06.260
I would have been able to buy it at a lower 
price if you had come a week earlier.

09:08.940 --> 09:10.760
I am thirsty.

09:10.760 --> 09:11.900
Be patient!

09:16.280 --> 09:20.780
Well, even saints cannot live without water.

09:20.780 --> 09:24.540
Would you like some water? 
Or perhaps some wine?

09:24.540 --> 09:26.620
May I have some water?

09:26.620 --> 09:29.090
Please wait a moment.

09:41.470 --> 09:44.170
The pepper is equal to forty-five weights.

09:44.170 --> 09:45.930
Where was this pepper produced?

09:46.230 --> 09:49.900
It was obtained from Ramapata 
in the Kingdom of Leedon.

09:49.900 --> 09:52.530
The Milone Trading Company 
contracted the import.

09:52.900 --> 09:58.750
From Ramapata? This pepper 
has traveled a long way.

09:59.160 --> 10:01.910
It seems the certificate is genuine.

10:02.220 --> 10:08.080
How about one Lumione gold coin 
for each weight here?

10:08.080 --> 10:11.040
What is the current market rate 
of Lumione gold coins?

10:11.040 --> 10:13.630
What is the principal currency 
you use, Mr. Lawrence?

10:13.630 --> 10:15.050
Trenni silver coins.

10:15.050 --> 10:20.990
One gold coin is worth 32 and 5/6 coins 
of Trenni silver in the current market.

10:26.350 --> 10:28.560
I accept that price.

10:29.470 --> 10:31.020
Thank you very much.

10:32.230 --> 10:33.230
What's wrong?

10:34.690 --> 10:36.180
I feel a bit dizzy...

10:36.180 --> 10:37.650
Are you all right?

10:39.100 --> 10:41.320
You must be exhausted from your travels.

10:41.320 --> 10:44.660
It seems my vision 
has suddenly tilted one way...

10:50.170 --> 10:55.260
Sir, it seems like I am still dizzy.

10:55.260 --> 10:56.960
Look, as you can see,

10:57.260 --> 11:00.970
everyone in front of me is leaning to one side.

11:14.210 --> 11:18.980
Now, did I drink water or wine?

11:21.260 --> 11:24.320
I must have consumed wine.

11:24.320 --> 11:25.810
Is that not right?

11:25.810 --> 11:30.970
They say that the livelier the tavern, 
the less the tavern owner drinks...

11:30.970 --> 11:34.240
I see. It seems that being the only 
sober person in the room

11:34.240 --> 11:37.300
is the key to a successful business.

11:37.300 --> 11:39.060
No, this is...

11:39.060 --> 11:42.180
It seems my companion and I are both drunk.

11:42.530 --> 11:46.780
So, I'm sure we will forget 
many things we saw and heard today.

11:47.170 --> 11:51.890
However, drunkards often 
make unreasonable demands.

11:51.890 --> 11:53.930
Wh-What do you mean?

11:53.930 --> 11:58.480
We'll receive what we deserve 
after the pepper is properly weighed and...

11:59.890 --> 12:01.240
Let's see...

12:02.370 --> 12:06.070
How about allowing me 
to buy twice its worth on credit?

12:06.070 --> 12:08.220
That is too much!

12:08.220 --> 12:13.290
Is that not possible? How unfortunate, 
it seems like I am growing sober.

12:16.510 --> 12:18.930
About the product I want...

12:18.930 --> 12:20.670
How about high-grade armor?

12:22.050 --> 12:23.510
Armor, you say?

12:23.900 --> 12:27.980
It is almost time for the yearly 
grand northern expedition.

12:27.980 --> 12:32.390
Armor is a standard risk-free 
and solid profit-making item.

12:32.390 --> 12:34.610
Armor...

12:34.610 --> 12:39.110
I'm sure you have a good relationship 
with some trading companies in Ruvinheigen.

12:39.110 --> 12:40.320
If I sell the armor to them,

12:40.320 --> 12:44.070
I should be able to pay you back 
immediately and offset the credit.

12:44.530 --> 12:45.810
How about it?

12:47.730 --> 12:49.360
Thank you very much.

12:49.360 --> 12:52.490
Then, please prepare the products 
as quickly as possible.

12:52.490 --> 12:54.160
I-I understand...

12:54.160 --> 12:56.830
What about the appraisal?

12:56.830 --> 12:58.570
I will leave it to you.

12:58.570 --> 13:01.050
After all, I have faith in God.

13:01.050 --> 13:05.010
Now, it seems I am growing sober as well.

13:05.010 --> 13:10.260
Some high-quality wine and dried 
sheep meat should suffice to please me.

13:10.260 --> 13:15.860
Th-There is a store that trades with me. 
Please take whatever you'd like from there.

13:15.860 --> 13:18.220
I will call for someone to guide you.

13:23.100 --> 13:24.620
I feel sorry for him.

13:24.620 --> 13:27.460
Even so, I'm surprised you noticed.

13:27.460 --> 13:31.120
My appearance, the coat of my tail, 
and my brain are all excellent,

13:31.120 --> 13:32.450
but so are my ears and eyes.

13:32.810 --> 13:36.000
I noticed the moment I entered the room.

13:36.000 --> 13:39.650
Well, it is enough to fool people like you.

13:39.650 --> 13:41.860
I can't argue with that.

13:43.060 --> 13:46.420
I am sure you will be fine 
on your own from here.

13:47.010 --> 13:49.760
I will go buy some food in the meantime.

13:50.180 --> 13:55.350
We must set off to Ruvinheigen as quickly 
as possible for the peaches pickled in honey!

13:58.190 --> 14:00.150
But just enough for us to reach Ruvinheigen.

14:01.010 --> 14:04.400
I know! Frugality, right?

14:15.170 --> 14:17.260
That took quite a while.

14:17.260 --> 14:19.610
Holo still isn't back?

14:21.650 --> 14:24.500
I hope this place doesn't go bankrupt 
due to her drinking tab.

14:24.500 --> 14:28.010
I heard when I was traveling in the north.

14:28.010 --> 14:32.910
The town that worshiped a pagan wolven god...

14:47.050 --> 14:48.500
That was delicious.

14:49.530 --> 14:51.380
Did you eat all of it?

14:51.380 --> 14:54.770
Be at ease. There is still plenty.

14:55.520 --> 14:58.490
Looks like you didn't practice any frugality.

14:58.490 --> 15:02.920
Well, now that my belly is full, 
I should groom my tail.

15:08.710 --> 15:10.070
That is right.

15:12.170 --> 15:13.300
What's the matter?

15:13.300 --> 15:17.330
I would like some oil 
once we reach the next town.

15:17.330 --> 15:18.140
Oil?

15:18.140 --> 15:23.190
Yes, I have heard it is good 
for maintaining my tail.

15:29.360 --> 15:30.950
Will you buy it for me?

15:32.420 --> 15:34.650
Have you ever calculated 
how much your clothes,

15:34.650 --> 15:37.010
shoes, travel expenses, 
alcohol and food expenses cost?

15:37.010 --> 15:39.850
Don't tell me that you're 
incapable of doing addition!

15:40.750 --> 15:43.000
I can add.

15:43.000 --> 15:46.240
Not only am I good at addition, 
but subtraction as well.

15:46.240 --> 15:50.420
Then it should be easy for 
the great Wise Wolf to guess my answer.

15:51.010 --> 15:53.060
Yes, I know.

15:53.060 --> 15:55.460
I am sure you will buy it for me.

15:55.890 --> 16:00.390
After all, you were able to make 
quite a profit because of me.

16:04.270 --> 16:06.740
Will you buy the oil?

16:06.740 --> 16:09.900
How much do you think you owe me by now?

16:09.900 --> 16:12.430
I'm not going to buy 
unnecessary items on top of that.

16:12.430 --> 16:17.200
Hm? You want me to return 
what I owe you that badly?

16:17.200 --> 16:19.260
Of course.

16:19.650 --> 16:22.690
I did not know you thought that way.

16:22.690 --> 16:24.370
Wh-What do you mean?

16:24.370 --> 16:30.020
Well, I will be free once I have paid you back.

16:30.920 --> 16:33.370
Then, I will hurry north.

16:34.190 --> 16:36.670
I hope Paro and Myuri are doing well.

16:39.380 --> 16:41.990
There isn't a deadline for your debt.

16:42.460 --> 16:45.660
Just pay me back before you 
reach the northern forests.

16:46.150 --> 16:47.340
How's that?

16:48.820 --> 16:49.610
Yes.

16:50.100 --> 16:54.810
I should be able to pay you back 
by the time I reach the northern forests.

16:54.810 --> 16:56.280
So, well...

16:56.280 --> 16:57.700
The oil?

16:58.370 --> 17:00.160
Will you buy it for me?

17:05.250 --> 17:06.500
Thank you.

17:13.450 --> 17:15.810
Why did you choose armor of all things?

17:15.810 --> 17:18.210
Ruvinheigen is the central hub 
for the great northern expedition,

17:18.210 --> 17:21.010
which is an expedition to hunt down heretics.

17:21.010 --> 17:23.400
Armor sells really well.

17:23.400 --> 17:25.600
Then, you should be making a big profit.

17:25.600 --> 17:30.520
No, there are a lot of merchants who provide 
armor, which in turn, lowers the price.

17:30.520 --> 17:33.500
But should this not be enough 
to make some profit?

17:33.500 --> 17:36.110
Well, we should make enough to afford your oil.

17:36.110 --> 17:40.600
But, all things considered, 
spices are definitely the best.

17:40.600 --> 17:42.060
To eat?

17:42.060 --> 17:44.870
I'm not like you. 
I'm talking about profits.

17:45.850 --> 17:48.750
Then you should have exchanged for more spices.

17:48.750 --> 17:52.560
The price of pepper doesn't change much 
between Poroson and Ruvinheigen.

17:52.560 --> 17:54.850
I'd lose out because of the tariffs.

17:54.850 --> 17:58.540
If I could find something 
as lucrative or better than spices,

17:58.540 --> 18:00.600
I'd be able to open up a store right away.

18:00.600 --> 18:02.410
Is there not something else?

18:02.410 --> 18:06.270
For instance, jewels or gold?

18:06.670 --> 18:10.680
Things like that aren't 
very profitable in Ruvinheigen.

18:10.680 --> 18:11.880
Why is that?

18:11.880 --> 18:16.570
If you try to import gold in Ruvinheigen, 
you get charged with an enormous tariff.

18:16.570 --> 18:20.050
Do the people in this town not want gold?

18:20.050 --> 18:20.910
That's not it.

18:20.910 --> 18:25.290
Only merchants who have connections 
with the Church are allowed to import gold.

18:25.610 --> 18:28.860
They get to pay a much 
lower tariff than others.

18:30.040 --> 18:31.130
On top of that,

18:31.130 --> 18:35.850
they can get the seal of the Church carved 
into the gold at Ruvinheigen's holy cathedral.

18:35.850 --> 18:39.590
That gold becomes "sacred gold" 
and rises a ridiculous amount in price.

18:39.590 --> 18:45.660
In other words, the Church and certain 
merchants are monopolizing all the profits.

18:45.660 --> 18:46.700
You guessed right.

18:46.700 --> 18:49.850
That is too filthy to be called sacred.

18:50.350 --> 18:53.120
Well, if you could join the secret circle,

18:53.120 --> 18:55.610
you'd be able to sell it ten times 
higher than it's actually worth.

18:55.610 --> 18:57.940
How about smuggling it in?

18:57.940 --> 19:00.500
Everyone would be doing that 
if that were possible.

19:00.500 --> 19:03.720
If you get caught, you lose your 
dominant arm, at the very least.

19:03.720 --> 19:06.560
The reward isn't worth the risk.

19:06.560 --> 19:08.160
That is true.

19:08.160 --> 19:11.050
Well, you have a solid business plan.

19:11.050 --> 19:13.380
It is better to save up your money 
the honest way.

19:13.380 --> 19:16.460
Well, there's someone using up 
all my hard-earned money...

19:16.930 --> 19:17.590
Hey.

19:18.750 --> 19:20.760
There are a lot of people ahead.

19:20.760 --> 19:21.550
Huh?

19:24.850 --> 19:27.970
If we take this detour, 
we'll end up on the holy road of Lyne...

19:27.970 --> 19:29.890
What do you think of this weave?

19:29.890 --> 19:33.020
Does anyone speak Palucian here?

19:36.220 --> 19:37.770
It seems like on the road ahead of us...

19:37.770 --> 19:41.400
Mercenary troops from the north 
are moving southward.

19:41.400 --> 19:45.080
There is a detour, but it's filled 
with wandering wolves.

19:45.080 --> 19:50.070
On top of that, there's been rumors of 
a pagan sorcerer that can summon wolves.

19:52.940 --> 19:55.580
So, what would the Wise Wolf Holo like to do?

19:56.690 --> 20:00.140
I have no fond memories of mercenaries.

20:00.140 --> 20:02.730
Well, mercenaries are a problem 
no matter there they go.

20:03.410 --> 20:04.800
What about the wolves on the detour?

20:04.800 --> 20:07.720
Hmph. They will be easier 
to handle than humans.

20:07.720 --> 20:10.090
At the very least, I can talk to them.

20:10.090 --> 20:11.250
Then it's decided.

20:16.400 --> 20:18.080
There's no one around.

20:18.080 --> 20:21.640
The power of rumors is quite formidable.

20:21.640 --> 20:22.860
Do you sense any wolves?

20:22.860 --> 20:29.650
We wolves are not foolish enough 
to be easily found in such an open area.

20:29.650 --> 20:30.330
However...

20:35.090 --> 20:38.460
A type of human I hate is ahead of us.

20:38.460 --> 20:40.840
The sorcerer? What should we do?

20:40.840 --> 20:43.210
It is the human's job to run.

20:44.190 --> 20:46.930
There is no need for us to avoid them.

20:59.770 --> 21:00.610
That's...

21:08.910 --> 21:10.030
A shepherd...

21:11.110 --> 21:14.910
So, the sorcerer is actually a shepherd.

21:27.760 --> 21:29.760
What was that just now?

21:29.760 --> 21:32.120
It's a ritual used when meeting a shepherd.

21:32.120 --> 21:35.270
Now I'm sure that person isn't a sorcerer.

21:38.130 --> 21:40.690
I am Lawrence, a traveling merchant.

21:40.690 --> 21:42.900
That is my traveling companion, Holo.

21:46.890 --> 21:49.970
I am sure that God 
has brought us together today.

21:49.970 --> 21:55.290
If you are a good shepherd, 
I know you will treat us appropriately.

